      "writtenOn": "2020-01-20T23:15:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is hard to understand: 1) why an IpRange (which is a contiguous block) needs to be converted into an IpPrefix. And 2) Why would there be more than one IpPrefix?\n\nIIUC, IpPrefix represents CIDR notation - so something like 1.2.3.4/24\nwhereas, IpRange represents start and end IPs - so corresponding equivalent of given IpPrefix should be 1.2.3.0 (start) to 1.2.3.255 (end).\n\nSo, if I\u0027m converting an IpRange into an IpPrefix there should only be one right?\n\nI guess I\u0027m getting confused as to what the real use case is?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "53b96a19b8583b665e7dc40d61cebbb49c5287e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
