      "writtenOn": "2020-01-21T01:33:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "for (1), Linux and Android routing systems both work based on prefixes, rather than ranges\n(2), ranges spanning multiple prefixes are possible:\n\n192.0.2.4 - 192.0.3.1 spans multiple prefixes:\n\n192.0.2.128/25\n192.0.2.64/26\n192.0.2.32/27\n192.0.2.16/28\n192.0.2.8/29\n192.0.2.4/30\n192.0.3.0/31",
